List-Id: linux-rdma@vger.kernel.org

Update mad.h to include umad_types.h and use the umad
definitions.  The data type names in mad.h are kept for
backwards compatibility, until all applications update
to using the umad names.

Signed-off-by: Sean Hefty <sean.hefty-ral2JQCrhuEAvxtiuMwx3w@public.gmane.org>
---
This change obviously requires updated libibumad header files.  I don't know
if you want to support older versions of the header files or not.  If so,
then it may be simplest to drop this patch.

Some sort of coordination may be needed on where the definition for ntohll
goes.

 include/infiniband/mad.h |  202 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 1 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 112 deletions(-)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 include/infiniband/mad.h

